WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.088
The rest of the gaps are about
the cloud and the record.

2
00:00:03.088 --> 00:00:07.818
The role's token is for commercial Resource
Manager, which is right for this estate,

3
00:00:07.818 --> 00:00:10.740
so the role-based playbook
refuses any other cloud,

4
00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.662
and a separate playbook
handles Azure Government.

5
00:00:13.662 --> 00:00:17.245
The token is briefly visible
on the server's command line;

6
00:00:17.245 --> 00:00:20.675
the chapter accepts that,
since tokens are short-lived.

7
00:00:20.675 --> 00:00:23.253
Nothing checks the region
against the cloud,

8
00:00:23.253 --> 00:00:27.225
nothing is written down, and Learn's
setup installs whatever's newest.

9
00:00:27.225 --> 00:00:32.210
The verdict: use Microsoft's role,
unchanged, and put the checks around it.
